{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And also Lot, etc.</b> Since indeed the main purpose of his pursuit was for Lot's sake, and Lot was the one he should have mentioned first, Scripture informs us of the order of successes in the manner of ״not only this, but also that״: first, that he restored the property of the kings — the first success; second, that he restored Lot — and the kings had not burned him when they saw him in battle against Avraham taking vengeance. And Scripture informs us that he set his mind to restore the men and the little ones, in honor of Lot."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:41:09.514007064Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}